{title:BNR one-off report Step 2: Approve the candidate}

{title:What this step does}

{pstd}
Step 2 records human approval of the exact one-off report candidate reviewed
after Step 1. It creates a public-ready package but does not publish it.

{title:Before you run it}

{pstd}
Review the complete candidate, including the PDF, landing page, metadata and
any associated data package. Complete and record the disclosure review.

{title:What to enter}

{phang}{bf:Study ID and version} must match the reviewed Step 1 candidate.

{phang}{bf:Full name and role} identify the authorised approver.

{phang}{bf:Review confirmations} must be ticked only after each stated action
has actually been completed.

{title:After running}

{pstd}
Confirm that the candidate is approved but not yet published and that the
approval receipt and manifest were created. Continue to one-off report Step 3
only when publication is authorised.

{title:Full instructions}

{pstd}
See the {browse "https://uwi-bnr.github.io/info-hub/technical/workflows/reporting/one-off-report.html":Technical Manual: Prepare, approve and publish a one-off CVD report}.
